## 3. Notes on Baseline (`B0 + B1 + B2`) Verification

- **Why `[PROFILE]` shows 22 dispatches (vs 21 prior to `d6f70fb`)**:
  - Commit `d6f70fb` lowered `D3dDevice::fill`'s upload-ring `staged()` threshold to `<= 256` bytes so the per-frame 50 KB `flow_` clear (`Engine::record_net`) executes via GPU `clear_range.spv` (`~1.5 us`) instead of a PCIe DMA copy. `[PROFILE]` reports both `sum` (all 22 dispatches) and `net21_sum` (the 21 network/post dispatches excluding `clear_range.spv`).
- **B0 & K2 Deterministic SPIR-V Hash Gate**:
  - `test_asi_units.exe` computes the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the 5 shipped Top-5 SPIR-V binaries in `build/asi/stage/openrr-amd/shaders/` and asserts `h_ship == h_nopad && h_ship != h_pad16k` (`spv_hash_nopad=EXACT`), deterministically catching any accidental re-enablement of `LDS_OCC_PAD`.
- **B1 Isolated Lossless Fast-Mode Pooling in `t0` (`attr_` Tail) + Wide Path (`<= +16 B/px`) + Sequential `0dc2625` Negative Control**:
  - Because `enc2 .. dec2_1` execute concurrently without barriers in flow mode, `enc_l_[1].pooled` and `enc_l_[1].dfn_pool` at the start of `f0` remain live during the flow chain. Placing `dec1_l_[2..4].tensor` and `dec1_l_[1..4].dfn` in the unused tail of `t0` (`px0 * 42.4 .. px0 * 46.6 < px0 * 48`, after all `enc_l_[1..5]` sub-buffers and `dec1_l_[1].tensor`, and above `dec_head_32_64`'s `px0 * 40` `headScratch`) avoids any address overlap with live flow inputs.
  - Fixed `dec0ScratchBytes` sizing (`dec0ScratchBytes = align256(dec0ScratchBytes) + px0 / 4 * 8` before `dec0_l_[1..4].tensor`) and enforced a runtime bounds assertion (`dOff <= dec0_l_[0].tensor.size && aOff <= attr_.size`).
  - Expanded `Engine::has_flow_buffer_overlap()` to check all 29 flow-concurrent sub-buffers pairwise (`enc_l_[0].dfn_pool`, `enc_l_[1].pooled/dfn_pool`, `enc_l_[2..5].tensor/dfn/pooled/dfn_pool`, `dec0_l_[1..4].tensor`, `dec1_l_[2..4].tensor/dfn`).
  - Restored in-place `wide` attribute replacement (`Engine::record_net` lines 635–664) using `dev_->create_unzeroed(needWide + 64)` (fully written by `enc0_attr_f_w` before `enc0_stage_32_64_f_w`, so no mid-frame `clear_range` dispatch is emitted), `dev_->destroy(sb)` (which defers actual `Release()` / `vkFreeMemory` in `grave_` until the active command list retires), and delta-shifting all `t0` sub-buffers including `dec1_l_[1..4].tensor` and `dec1_l_[1..4].dfn`. This keeps `wide` VRAM overhead at `<= +16 B/px` (`+5.68 MB` at 1080p Quality, `+22.21 MB` at 4K Quality).
  - Verified in isolation (same binary, `set_pool_dec1_tail(false)` vs `set_pool_dec1_tail(true)` across 20 frames x 2 runs, with frames 10..14 exercising the `wide` `depth_of_field` path, plus a negative-control run `set_pool_dec1_f0_race_for_test(true)` that sequentially places `dec1_l_[2..4].tensor` at `f0+0` via `sub(f0, d1Off, ...)` exactly matching the `0dc2625` buggy layout):
    - 1080p: `diff_vs_unpooled=0 (max_ulp_diff=0), repeat_diff=0, flow_overlap_audit=CLEAN (neg_ctrl_f0_race_caught=YES, race_diff=38875537), saved=1.44 MB, wide_vram_delta=+5.68 MB (<=+16 B/px)` (`252 -> 251 MB` feature, `-2.3 MB` `proc_delta`).
    - 4K: `diff_vs_unpooled=0 (max_ulp_diff=0), repeat_diff=0, flow_overlap_audit=CLEAN (neg_ctrl_f0_race_caught=YES, race_diff=153478994), saved=5.62 MB, wide_vram_delta=+22.21 MB (<=+16 B/px)` (`966 -> 960 MB` feature, `-6.7 MB` `proc_delta`).
- **B2 Lossy Fast-Mode Approximations, 3-Run Per-Macro A/B & Why 1080p Parity Matched `c671f57` Bit-for-Bit**:
  - 3-run interleaved per-macro A/B in `test_asi_units.exe` confirms:
    - `post_f_lt`: `+LT_POST_EXP=1 +LT_POST_NOCORNER=1 +LT_POST_NETH=1` improves 1080p 3-run median by `-6.4%` (`346.3 -> 324.2 us`, `-22.1 us`) and 4K 3-run median by `-6.1%` (`1497.1 -> 1405.6 us`, `-91.5 us`), whereas adding `LT_POST_LOG=1` slows down 1080p by `+7.8%` (`349.4 us`) and 4K by `+6.4%` (`1495.0 us`). **Enabled by default.**
    - `enc0_attr_f_lt`: `+LT_ATTR_RCP=1 +LT_ATTR_DEPTH=1` is within noise (`+2.4%` at 1080p `176.4 -> 180.6 us`, `-0.2%` at 4K `816.6 -> 814.6 us`), while `+LT_ATTR_SAME=1 +LT_ATTR_CL=1` slows down 1080p by `+34.8%` (`243.4 us`) and 4K by `+21.0%` (`985.8 us`). **Both disabled by default** per the rule that a lossy macro must clearly speed up both 1080p and 4K.
    - `C=64` (`enc_stage_64_64_96` + `dec_up_64_64_96` + `dec_dfn_64_64`): `+LT_FAR=3` is within noise at 1080p (`-0.5%`, `712.3 -> 709.1 us`) and slower at 4K (`+1.2%`, `2664.6 -> 2697.5 us`). **Disabled by default.**
  - **Why 1080p `openrr_bench` Parity is Bit-Identical Before and After Disabling `LT_ATTR_RCP=1 LT_ATTR_DEPTH=1` (while 1440p & 4K Changed)**:
    - FNV-1a 64-bit SPIR-V hashes confirm the shipped shaders changed when `LT_ATTR_RCP=1 LT_ATTR_DEPTH=1` was disabled (`enc0_attr_f_lt.spv`: `0x8ce69feb59494028` vs `+RCP+DEPTH` `0x542fa850a284dcf2`; `d3d_enc0_attr_f_lt.spv`: `0x322f982652279cf6` vs `+RCP+DEPTH` `0x4c6e3305ad708657`).
    - In `openrr_bench.cpp` (`UploadPattern` + `runOneFrame`), `mvData` is spatially uniform (`(0.25, -0.15)` at every pixel), so `LT_ATTR_DEPTH` (which selects `pmx` / `pmn` in a 3x3 neighborhood to fetch `mv_far = mv_at(pmx)` and `mv_near = mv_at(pmn)`) always fetches `(0.25, -0.15)` regardless of `pmx` / `pmn`.
    - Furthermore, `nData` is constant `(0, 0, 1)`, `world_to_view` is identity, and `view_to_clip` has `m[14] = 0.05 != 0, m[15] = 0`, so `C(0x460) = 1.0 >= 1.0` (`rcp_c(dz)` in `reflection_mv` is bypassed). And because `cData` is identical on every frame, auto-exposure `pc.expo.v[1]` converges to a single scalar `0.5068359375` where `1.0f / x == rcp_rn(x)` in FP32.
    - The only remaining uses of `rcp_c` / `sqrt_c` are in `reflection_mv` (`w = 1.0` so `rcp_c(w) == 1.0`) and `l1` / `l2` motion consistency. At 1080p (`1280x720 -> 1920x1080`), the upscaling ratio is `1920 / 1280 = 1.5` and `1080 / 720 = 1.5` (exact dyadic floats `C(0x2f8) = 2/3, C(0x300) = 1.5`), and after `ATTR64` blue-noise dither + truncation to a 9-bit FP8-like mantissa (`3` mantissa bits), every pixel at `1280x720` produces the exact same 48-byte `ATTR64` record with or without `LT_ATTR_RCP`. At 1440p (`1706x960 -> 2560x1440`, where `2560 / 1706 = 1.50058615...` is non-dyadic) and 4K (`2560x1440 -> 3840x2160`, `3.68M` grid pixels), a small number of pixels sit within `1 ULP` of a 9-bit dither rounding boundary in `reflection_mv`, flipping `differing` from `8,740,474 -> 8,753,693` at 1440p and `13,851,894 -> 13,842,962` at 4K.
  - **Note on 1080p vs 4K Kernel-Sum vs End-to-End Delta**:
    - At **1080p**, `post_f_lt` saves `~20-22 us` (`346.3 -> 324.2 us`) and `B0` (`LDS_OCC_PAD` removal) is within `~0-5 us` noise (`nopad=1024.6 us` vs `occ_pad_16KB=1022.5 us`), whereas the 3-run same-process end-to-end median improved by **`-47 us` (`3.171 -> 3.124 ms`, `-1.5%`)** — the end-to-end gain exceeds the isolated kernel sum by `~25-30 us` (unattributed across per-dispatch timestamp serialization / cache state).
    - At **4K**, `post_f_lt` saves `~91 us` (`1497.1 -> 1405.6 us`) and `B0` (`LDS_OCC_PAD` removal on W1) saves `~60-76 us` (`4189.5 -> 4113.6 us`), totaling `~151-167 us` at the kernel level, which roughly matches the 3-run same-process end-to-end median improvement of **`-129 us` (`11.941 -> 11.812 ms`, `-1.1%`)**.

